  "section_notes": "S2 keeps the 55 °C/5% benchmark but removes any sales stop, so a model above 5% can keep selling after regulator review, and S5 makes recall discretionary with the 8-per-100k figure serving only as a trigger for assessment, which favours the Halcyon flagship. S3 sets new-unit shut-off at 24 months and leaves retrofit with no stated upper deadline (only a floor of 6 years), which favours Northwind's low-shut-off installed base. S4's 36-month suppression start is within the acceptable range and S1's reporting timelines are acceptable, though the S1 'confirmed incidents' scope is a gap."
